 characters</article-title><source>Genetics</source><year>1950</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>212</fpage><lpage>235</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17247344</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vinson</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Kliewer</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Overall classification as a selection criterion for improving categorically scored components of type in Holsteins</article-title><source>J Dairy Sci</source><year>1976</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>2104</fpage><lpage>2114</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stock</surname><given-names>KF</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamann</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Distl</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Estimation of genetic parameters for the prevalence of osseous fragments in limb joints of Hanoverian Warmblood horses</article-title><source>J Anim Breed Genet</source><year>2005</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>280</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16060495</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1439-0388.2005.00527.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dekkers</surname><given-names>JCM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Commercial application of marker- and gene-assisted selection in livestock: strategies and lessons</article-title><source>J Anim Sci (E Suppl)</source><year>2004</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>E313</fpage><lpage>E328</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>B&#x000f6;neker</surname><gi